                <tr id="issuerow12417010" rel="12417010" data-issuekey="IVY-1050" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1050" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1050">IVY-1050</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Fail the retrieve when multiple artifacts of same module are mapped to same file
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Mar/09 23:22 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 17/Mar/09 22:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 16/Mar/09 23:27 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If the retrieve job maps different artifacts of the same module to the same filename, Ivy should throw an error.<br/>
This would solve problems when retrieving artifacts from the maven repositories where also sources/javadocs artifacts exists and where the retrieve pattern doesn&#39;t distinguish between them (doesn&#39;t contain a [type] or [classifier] token). At the moment, a random selected artifact is being retrieved, which results in unpredictable builds...<br/>
<br/>
The behaviour when multiple artifacts of different modules are mapped to the same file should remain as is to keep backwards compatibility as much as possible: a conflictmanager selects the most recent artifact.
  </td>
