                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-1115                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I had the following situation:<br/>
<br/>
#A;working-&gt; { #B;[1.0] #C;[2.0,2.5] }<br/>
#B;1.0-&gt;#C;2.1<br/>
<br/>
#B and #C have extra attributes in the &lt;info/&gt; section.<br/>
All &lt;dependencies/&gt; use the force attribute.<br/>
<br/>
When I resolve and deliver A using the latest-compatible conflict manager, I expect to see #C;2.1 in my deliver IVY file. However, I am seeing #C;[2.0,2.5]<br/>
<br/>
Attached are 2 tests. One which uses a file repository with ivy files for #B and #C with no extra attributes. One which does not.<br/>
<br/>
Thanks,<br/>
<br/>
Scott<br/>
<br/>

