                                            <td class="environment">      MacOS 10.5.7 with newest Apple Java -- but this issue deals with tarfile contents.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The downloadable tarball apache-ivy-2.1.0-rc1-src.tar.gz does not contain a .classpath.default file. This causes the &#39;eclipse-default&#39; build target to fail. <br/>
There are other dot-files in the Subversion repository&#39;s tags/2.1.0-rc1 directory which are absent in the source tarball, e.g. classpath.ivyde and build-release.xml. <br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m fairly new to Ivy, so I don&#39;t know if the source tarball is *supposed* to contain just a subset of the repository contents; however, it appears to do that.
