                <tr id="issuerow12433516" rel="12433516" data-issuekey="IVY-1113" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1113" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1113">IVY-1113</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                offer option to suppress output during Ivy deliver
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mitch Gitman
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mitch Gitman
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 19/Aug/09 21:20 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Aug/09 15:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        unspecified            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        unspecified            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Whenever Ivy successfully delivers an Ivy file, you see two lines of output that begin with the following:<br/>
:: delivering :: ...<br/>
    delivering ivy file to ...<br/>
<br/>
This output is produced by Message.info calls in the deliver method of DeliverEngine (lines 103 and 179 respectively).<br/>
<br/>
What I&#39;m asking for is for this output to be conditionally suppressed. <br/>
<br/>
It seems that implementation-wise, this would be easy enough to accomplish. I see that both the ResolveOptions and DownloadOptions classes extend LogOptions. LogOptions has a LOG_QUIET flag. What about just making the DeliverOptions class extend LogOptions as well? Then have those two Message.info invocations be conditional on:<br/>
!LogOptions.LOG_QUIET.equals(deliver.getOptions().getLog())<br/>
<br/>
Whether this option should be extended to another API level, such as the deliver Ant task, is another question. But I&#39;d be satisfied with just the above programmatic API change.
  </td>
