                <tr id="issuerow12445009" rel="12445009" data-issuekey="IVY-1158" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1158" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1158">IVY-1158</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Make ivy.xml &lt;conf description&gt; available
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jan Matèrne
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jan Matèrne
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Jan/10 09:37 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 07/May/10 20:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 12/Jan/10 14:44 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      You can (an IMHO should) write an explanation of the configuration in the ivy file<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;2.0&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;configurations&gt;<br/>
        &lt;conf name=&quot;runtime&quot; description=&quot;Runtime Libraries&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/configurations&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivy-module&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The Ant task &lt;ivy:info/&gt; makes the names names available, but not the descriptions. <br/>
So the first RFE is making them available (accoding to &#39;infotest.configurations&#39;) as &#39;infotest.configuration.descriptions&#39;.<br/>
<br/>
Another RFE is enhanding &lt;ivy:retrieve/&gt; to create a describing file in the destination directory which contains this information.<br/>
E.e. with Ivy pattern lib/[conf]/[artifact].[ext] you would create with &lt;ivy:retrieve descriptionfile=&quot;readme.txt&quot;/&gt; a file lib/runtime/readme.txt with content &quot;Runtime Libraries&quot;.<br/>
(!! Recreate old files, but beware that multiple confs could result in the same dir if the ivy pattern doesnt contain a [conf]. )<br/>

  </td>
