</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I need to use a different revision scheme that looks like R1A01, i.e. not the normal scheme x.y.z, for my company internal dependencies. When doing this, I discovered that ApacheURLLister does not handle directories without a dot (.) properly as it filters those out. If it does not find a dot in the directory name, it compares the href with the text but forgets to check for a trailing slash in href.
