                <tr id="issuerow12465381" rel="12465381" data-issuekey="IVY-1193" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1193" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1193">IVY-1193</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Trying to move Ivy to an HTTP-based publish model, we discovered that it doesn&#39;t perform a MKCOL before doing a PUT.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ervin Beba
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ervin Beba
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/May/10 14:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 01/Jul/12 22:41 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-1307                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      All environments.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The problem is that when Ivy attempts to publish to a URL resolver via HTTP, it does not adhere to the WebDav requirement that you create the parent path (parent collections) with a MKCOL command before the PUT command. Ivy incorrectly just attempts to PUT artifacts to a path which hasn&#39;t been created.
  </td>
