<br/>
In our environment, a bunch of files from repo1.maven.org are cached in the squid. So there were a lot of conflicts with content encoding.<br/>
<br/>
The possible workarounds:<br/>
1. Check returned content encoding from http client, if it is not identity, reissue the request with disabling the caches.<br/>
2. Ungzip files fetched with gzip content encoding.<br/>
3. Support gzip content encoding in common HTTP.<br/>
3. Use local maven proxies <br/>

