                <tr id="issuerow12478005" rel="12478005" data-issuekey="IVY-1240" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1240" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1240">IVY-1240</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Only the last dependency descriptor is taken into account on the same module
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Nicolas Lalevée
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Nicolas Lalevée
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Nicolas Lalevée
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 21/Oct/10 16:18 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 21/Oct/10 16:47 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 21/Oct/10 16:47 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In some of our project we had:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;dependency org=&quot;org&quot; name=&quot;mymodule&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; conf=&quot;compile,runtime-&gt;conf1&quot; /&gt;<br/>
&lt;dependency org=&quot;org&quot; name=&quot;mymodule&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; conf=&quot;compile,runtime-&gt;conf2&quot; /&gt;<br/>
&lt;dependency org=&quot;org&quot; name=&quot;mymodule&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; conf=&quot;compile,runtime-&gt;conf3&quot; /&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
When resolving dependencies with the conf &quot;*&quot;, the resulting &quot;compile&quot; conf report did contain dependencies of the conf1, conf2 and conf3 of mymodule. But the resulting &quot;runtime&quot; conf report, contained only the configuration of conf3 of mymodule.<br/>
<br/>
Changing the dependency into the following one fixed it:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;dependency org=&quot;org&quot; name=&quot;mymodule&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; conf=&quot;compile,runtime-&gt;conf1,conf2,conf3&quot; /&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>

  </td>
