</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently buildlist does not support revisions while filtering leafs and roots.<br/>
<br/>
The leaf and root attribute should handle specifying revisions (and even organizations) in the form of (org#module#revision,org#module#revision,...) and should return a list also of the form (org#module#revision,org#module#revision,...).<br/>
This is crucial when new dependencies are introduced in new releases of a certain project.<br/>
<br/>
A use case for this is in continuous integration scripts, where a change in a certain org1#module1#revision1 should trigger a recompilation of a dependent org2#module2#revision2 (All other org2#module2 projects should not need rebuilding)
  </td>
