                                            <td class="environment">      mac os x, with java 1.6.0_22, ivy trunk, and maven 2.2.1.  have experienced this issue also with windows 7, java 1.6.0_18 and ivy 2.1.0.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Given the maven dependencies:<br/>
<br/>
C has parent P<br/>
P specifies dependency management of T:1.0 (not specifying scope, or type)<br/>
P specifies dependency management of T:1.0:test for type test-jar<br/>
C depends on T<br/>
<br/>
when:<br/>
I create an ivy.xml that depends on C<br/>
<br/>
Then:<br/>
Ivy cannot resolve the transitive dependency of T in the default configuration.  Maven will resolve T as a compile scoped dependency.<br/>

  </td>
