                <tr id="issuerow12508477" rel="12508477" data-issuekey="IVY-1296" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1296" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1296">IVY-1296</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                dual resolver without @name gives NPE
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Leigh L. Klotz, Jr
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Leigh L. Klotz, Jr
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/May/11 21:11 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 26/May/11 21:12 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      A &lt;dual&gt; with no name attribute gets an NPE in resolve.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;dual&gt; says it uses common attributes.  If so, it really should check and complain instead of blowing up cryptically.<br/>
<br/>
Here&#39;s a test-caseish description:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivysettings&gt;<br/>
 &lt;settings defaultResolver=&quot;x&quot; /&gt;<br/>
 &lt;resolvers&gt;<br/>
    &lt;chain name=&quot;vendor-1&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;dual &gt;<br/>
        &lt;filesystem name=&quot;vendor1-ivy&quot; checkmodified=&quot;true&quot; changingPattern=&quot;.*&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;ivy pattern=&quot;${vendor.dir}/vendor1-ivy/[organization]-ivy.xml&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
        &lt;filesystem name=&quot;vendor1-jars&quot; checkmodified=&quot;true&quot; changingPattern=&quot;.*&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${vendor.dir}/vendor1/[artifact].[ext]&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dual&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/chain&gt;<br/>
    &lt;chain name=&quot;x&quot;&gt; ... &lt;/chain&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/resolvers&gt;<br/>
  &lt;modules&gt;<br/>
    &lt;module organisation=&quot;com.vendor1&quot; module=&quot;*&quot; resolver=&quot;vendor1&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/modules&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivysettings&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
 vendor1&#39;s module object has a resolver with no name, and it gets an NPE trying to cache that name inside DefaultRepositoryCacheManager.saveResolvers.<br/>
<br/>
main[1] where<br/>
  [1] java.util.Hashtable.put (Hashtable.java:394)<br/>
  [2] java.util.Properties.setProperty (Properties.java:143)<br/>
  [3] org.apache.ivy.core.cache.DefaultRepositoryCacheManager.saveResolvers (DefaultRepositoryCacheManager.java:423)<br/>
  [4] org.apache.ivy.core.resolve.IvyNode.loadData (IvyNode.java:176)<br/>
  [5] org.apache.ivy.core.resolve.VisitNode.loadData (VisitNode.java:287)<br/>
  [6] org.apache.ivy.core.resolve.ResolveEngine.fetchDependencies (ResolveEngine.java:696)<br/>
