</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      WinXP
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the &lt;dependencies&gt; section of ivy.xml I have a number of &lt;dependency&gt; elements and one &lt;exlude&gt; element. If I do not put the &lt;exclude&gt; right at the end of the section, the Ant ivy:resolve task throws a ParseException (see attached stack trace).<br/>
<br/>
I will attach simple examples of ok and failing ivy.xml files.<br/>
<br/>
This seems like a bug to me, but even if it is expected behaviour, at least a note in the manual would be nice.
