                <tr id="issuerow12514383" rel="12514383" data-issuekey="IVY-1306" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1306" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1306">IVY-1306</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Problem with wildcards in defaultconf attribute
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Marc De Boeck
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Marc De Boeck
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 17/Jul/11 20:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 17/Jul/11 20:10 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP, Java 6, ant 1.8.2
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the ivy.xml file of a module, I have the following configurations and dependencies:<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;configurations&gt;<br/>
      &lt;conf name=&quot;compile&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;conf name=&quot;test&quot; extends=&quot;compile&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;conf name=&quot;rad&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;conf name=&quot;ear&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;conf name=&quot;wsdl&quot;/&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/configurations&gt;<br/>
    &lt;dependencies defaultconfmapping=&quot;* -&gt; #&quot; defaultconf=&quot;*,!wsdl&quot; &gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;org1&quot; name=&quot;mod1&quot; conf=&quot;wsdl -&gt; conf1&quot; rev=&quot;latest.integration&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;org1&quot; name=&quot;mod2&quot; rev=&quot;latest.integration&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/dependencies&gt;<br/>
       <br/>
mod1 and mod2 have the same configurations as the parent module above.<br/>
       <br/>
In the build file, I do the following to resolve and retrieve the artifacts for this parent module:<br/>
<br/>
            &lt;ivy:resolve conf=&quot;ear&quot; /&gt;<br/>
            &lt;ivy:retrieve pattern=&quot;${project.target.lib.dir}/[artifact].[ext]&quot; sync=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;ear&quot;/&gt;<br/>
                        &lt;ivy:report conf=&quot;ear&quot; ... /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
It seems that for modules such as mod2, I retrieve artifacts from all configurations (except the conf &quot;wsdl&quot;) and not just the ear-configuration.<br/>
The attribute &quot;defaultconf&quot; seems to be responsible for that.<br/>
This can also be seen in the output of ivy:report.<br/>
For mod2, I can see that it returns the following configurations:<br/>
Configurations: test, compile, rad, ear, * <br/>
<br/>
When I change the defaultconf attribute to:<br/>
    &lt;dependencies defaultconfmapping=&quot;* -&gt; #&quot; defaultconf=&quot;compile,rad,ear&quot; &gt;<br/>
Then the resolve works as expected.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
