                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Some Maven repo servers will respond with an HTTP 204 (no content) when a HEAD request is made for a resource. For example:<br/>
{code}<br/>
curl -I http://teleal.org/m2/org/teleal/cling/cling-core/1.0.5/cling-core-1.0.5.pom<br/>
{code}<br/>
will respond with a 204. Ivy&#39;s BasicURLHandler class will treat this as a failed lookup.
