                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Mac OS X Lion 10.7.2, MacPorts, 2011 MacBook Pro with Intel Core i7.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The /localivy target does not work when building Ivy jar (ant /localivy jar). It is supposed to result in ivy.home being set to $BUILD/.ivy2 instead of $HOME/.ivy2. However, it fails to do so, at least when building the jar target (and probably others). In MacPorts, this causes problems, as Ivy is built as an unprivileged user different to the real user, so can&#39;t access ~/.ivy2/cache, so can&#39;t resolve dependencies, and the whole build fails.
  </td>
