                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 7, Ant 1.8.1, Ivy 2.2.1.alpha_20120313100444
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      This is a followup bug to IVY-1233.  With IVY-1233 fixed in the trunk, the conflict manager no longer infinite loops, but on an unresolved conflict, its not erroring, instead an exception is occurred.<br/>
<br/>
Repro:<br/>
A (being built) Depends on B pVer.main.+, C \[1.0,2.0\[, D \[1.5,1.7\[<br/>
B pVer.main.0.0 Depends on D \[1.6.1,2.0\[<br/>
B 1.0.0 Depends on D \[1.6.1,2.0\[<br/>
B 1.1.0 Depends on D \[1.6.1,2.0\[<br/>
C 1.0.0 Depends on B \[1.0,2.0\[, D \[1.6.0,1.7\[<br/>
C 1.1.0 Depends on B \[1.1,2.0\[, D \[1.6.0,1.7\[<br/>
D no Dependencies<br/>
<br/>
The dependency on B is not resolvable since A and C don&#39;t agree on revision ranges.<br/>
<br/>
Expected:<br/>
Error stating the module(s) that could not be resolved.<br/>
<br/>
Actual:<br/>
Exception complaining about unrelated module.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

