ANT_HOME=C:\tools\apache-ant-1.6.5<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      this is an example of my ivy.xml:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;dependency org=&quot;org1&quot; name=&quot;module1&quot; rev=&quot;1.0.0&quot;&gt;<br/>
		&lt;artifact name=&quot;lib1-1.0.0&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
	  <br/>
   &lt;dependency org=&quot;org1&quot; name=&quot;module1&quot; rev=&quot;1.0.0&quot;&gt;<br/>
			&lt;artifact name=&quot;lib2-1.0.0&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; /&gt;<br/>
   &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
with ivy 1.0.0 I can download both artifatcs<br/>
<br/>
when I upgrade my version to ivy-2.0.0<br/>
<br/>
only one of the artifact is downloaded.<br/>
<br/>
is there something in ivy settings I must specified ?<br/>
I know that if I write the file like this:<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;dependency org=&quot;org1&quot; name=&quot;module1&quot; rev=&quot;1.0.0&quot;&gt;<br/>
		&lt;artifact name=&quot;lib1-1.0.0&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; /&gt;<br/>
		&lt;artifact name=&quot;lib2-1.0.0&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
	  <br/>
 it works !<br/>
<br/>
But why not the first example? <br/>
there&#39;s a workaround?<br/>

  </td>
