                                            <td class="environment">      Linux using with ant 1.8.0
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      According to here http://ant.apache.org/ivy/history/latest-milestone/concept.html#patterns<br/>
<br/>
[originalname] (since 1.4)<br/>
the original artifact name (including the extension) <br/>
<br/>
What I am seeing however is that originalname is the artifact name with the final file level .&lt;ext&gt; removed.  It is not even the actual defined [ext] pattern that is removed.<br/>
<br/>
For example, for eclipse compatibility, we have source jars in our internal repository with ext=&quot;src.jar&quot;, so the filename is artifact.src.jar I see the originalname when used is artifact.src and when I set my cache pattern as [originalname].[ext] in trying to work around this, I get artifact.src.src.jar
  </td>
