                <tr id="issuerow12596080" rel="12596080" data-issuekey="IVY-1361" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1361" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1361">IVY-1361</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Updatesite resolver will download a feature jar if the name matches the plugin jar it should actually be downloading
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Nicolas Lalevée
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Christopher Frost
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Christopher Frost
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Jun/12 13:07 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Jun/12 13:52 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Jun/12 13:52 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.3.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.0-RC2            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Simple command line ant build with Apache Ant(TM) version 1.8.2 compiled on December 20 2010. No other plugins other than Ivy 2.3.0-RC1
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When resolving a bundle against a p2 repository using the updatesite resolver, it is downloading a jar file from the features directory that has the same file name as the plugin it should be downloading from the plugins directory. I&#39;m doing this inline with the following command.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy:cachepath pathid=&quot;bundlor.classpath&quot; organisation=&quot;bundle&quot; module=&quot;org.eclipse.virgo.bundlor.ant&quot; revision=&quot;1.1.0.M05&quot; conf=&quot;default&quot; inline=&quot;true&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
There are no failures, it&#39;s just downloading the feature instead of the plugin bundle. I can&#39;t see what I&#39;ve done wrong, I haven&#39;t seen any mention of support for a features anywhere, would be great to have support for products and features as well though.<br/>
<br/>
Chris.
  </td>
