                                            <td class="environment">      Win 7, 64bit
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When ivy module (B) with &lt;exclude&gt; extends (http://ant.apache.org/ivy/history/latest-milestone/ivyfile/extends.html) parent module (A) with &lt;dependency&gt;, ivy descriptors are merged incorrectly.<br/>
<br/>
Error appears while resolve of other module (C ), which use module B (&lt;dependency&gt;), because task ivy:resolve validates ivy.xml of module B (merged incorrectly form A and B) against schema.<br/>
<br/>
Result:<br/>
[ivy:resolve] :: problems summary ::<br/>
		[ivy:resolve] :::: WARNINGS<br/>
		[ivy:resolve] 		::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::<br/>
		[ivy:resolve] 		::          UNRESOLVED DEPENDENCIES         ::<br/>
		[ivy:resolve] 		::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::<br/>
		[ivy:resolve] 		:: pl.com.max.poc#ivy-bug-module;1.0: java.text.ParseException: [xml parsing: ivy-1.0.xml.original:34:86: cvc-complex-type.2.4.a: Inva<br/>
		lid content was found starting with element &#39;dependency&#39;. One of &#39;{exclude, override, conflict}&#39; is expected. in file:/C:/Users/jwisniewski/.ivy2/cach<br/>
		e/pl.com.max.poc/ivy-bug-module/ivy-1.0.xml.original
  </td>
