                <tr id="issuerow12706703" rel="12706703" data-issuekey="IVY-1466" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1466" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1466">IVY-1466</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                overwrite flag causes publish failure for repositories which autogenerate checksums
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Joshua Suereth
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Joshua Suereth
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 04/Apr/14 20:50 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Apr/14 21:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ubuntu, Artifactory (maven or ivy), server-generated checksums enabled (since maven also published to the repo)
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When publishing to a repository with &quot;overwrite&quot; set to false, Ivy publishes the artifact *then* checks to see if the checksum file exists.   Since Artifactory automatically creates the checksums, this leads to a failure to publish because the checksum already exists.<br/>
<br/>
I see two possible fixes:<br/>
<br/>
1) Publish signatures/checksums first (I think this may cause other issues with things like nexus/artifactory<br/>
2) If you succeed to publish the artifact with the correct overwrite flag, then ALWAYS overwrite when publishing the checksums (since you just pushed the artifact).  There&#39;s really no reason not to, and it could cause problems if you don&#39;t.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
We&#39;re taking option #2 in sbt, see our hacky workaround here: https://github.com/sbt/sbt/pull/1232/files#diff-b50b19f131fece36d762990bd9d34625R77
  </td>
