                <tr id="issuerow12707162" rel="12707162" data-issuekey="IVY-1467" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1467" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1467">IVY-1467</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Resolving results in weird working@[localhostname] revisions
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Duplicate
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ulrike M
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ulrike M
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Apr/14 11:53 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Jan/15 08:51 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 08/Jan/15 08:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.4.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">6</td>
                                            <td class="watches">7</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-1457                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I wanted to give 2.4.0-RC1 a try and ran into this issue. See the log for details.<br/>
<br/>
I stripped down the case to the bare minimum of what causes the error. If i specify the following dependencies, resolving conf=&#39;<br/>
runtime&#39; will fail with &quot;unresolved dependencies&quot;:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;dependency org=&quot;org.slf4j&quot; name=&quot;slf4j-api&quot; rev=&quot;1.7.7&quot; conf=&quot;compile-&gt;default&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;dependency org=&quot;org.slf4j&quot; name=&quot;slf4j-log4j12&quot; rev=&quot;1.7.7&quot; conf=&quot;runtime-&gt;default&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
(...)<br/>
:: log4j#log4j;working@PIT11: not found<br/>
(...)<br/>
<br/>
we are separating compile-time dependencies (slf4j-api) from runtime dependencies (slf4j-log4j12); this must be specified as two dependencies (as far as I know).<br/>
The funny thing is that if I alter the version of slf4j-api to &quot;1.7.6&quot;, clear the ivy cache and resolve again, it will work smoothly. Version 1.7.6 of slf4j-api will simply get evicted (as expected).<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
