                <tr id="issuerow12756012" rel="12756012" data-issuekey="IVY-1498" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1498" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1498">IVY-1498</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mixed use of symlinks leads to cache corruption
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Blocker
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Stephen Haberman
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Stephen Haberman
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Nov/14 04:38 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> 10/Jul/17 11:55 </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Sep/15 18:15 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If a user switches between &quot;use symlinks&quot; or not (or, say, has ant/ivy configured with symlinks but Eclipse/IvyDE without symlinks), the ivycache can be corrupted.<br/>
<br/>
Specifically, if a symlink was setup in symlink mode:<br/>
<br/>
lib/foo.jar --&gt; ivycache/com/foo/foo-1.2.jar<br/>
<br/>
And then later we retrieve into lib without symlink mode, Ivy retrieve will write, say, foo-1.3.jar&#39;s bytes into the lib/foo.jar location...which will then overwrite the foo-1.2.jar bytes in the ivycache.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
