                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      linux
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      According to the XDG specification [1], there is a better way to store the user specific data of an application by dumping in new hidden folder in ~/.<br/>
More information about it can be found [2]<br/>
<br/>
The specification defines places to store the data so that the user profile can be updated and moved properly while reducing some weird bugs.<br/>
Those places would be ~/.local/ivy or ~/.cache/ivy and other (depending on the data stored)<br/>
<br/>
[1]: http://standards.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest.html<br/>
[2]: https://ploum.net/207-modify-your-application-to-use-xdg-folders/
  </td>
