                <tr id="issuerow12782359" rel="12782359" data-issuekey="IVY-1516" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1516" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1516">IVY-1516</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Module that extends is not picking up exclude element(s) from parent&#39;s dependencies
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Eric Milles
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eric Milles
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Mar/15 20:49 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 16/Mar/15 21:40 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ivy 2.4.0, IvyDE 2.2.0.final, Ant 1.9.4
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have a base project that defines a number of configurations and dependencies, including a few exclude elements to prevent conflicting dependencies from coming in transitively.  In a child module, the configurations and dependencies are being inherited properly, but the excludes no longer take effect.<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;2.0&quot;<br/>
  xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;<br/>
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=&quot;http://ant.apache.org/ivy/schemas/ivy.xsd&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;info module=&quot;A&quot; organisation=&quot;com.org&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;configurations&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;local&quot; visibility=&quot;private&quot;<br/>
        description=&quot;Artifacts necessary for local development and testing&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;master&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/configurations&gt;<br/>
  &lt;dependencies defaultconf=&quot;master&quot; defaultconfmapping=&quot;*-&gt;master,runtime()&quot;&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;log4j&quot; name=&quot;log4j&quot; rev=&quot;1.2.17&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;org.slf4j&quot; name=&quot;slf4j-api&quot; rev=&quot;1.7.10&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;org.slf4j&quot; name=&quot;slf4j-log4j12&quot; rev=&quot;1.7.10&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency org=&quot;org.slf4j&quot; name=&quot;jcl-over-slf4j&quot; rev=&quot;1.7.10&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;!-- ensure logging flows through the chosen 4 by excluding potential interlopers --&gt;<br/>
        &lt;exclude conf=&quot;local&quot; matcher=&quot;regexp&quot; org=&quot;.*(commons-logging|logback|log4j|slf4j)&quot; /&gt;<br/>
        &lt;exclude conf=&quot;master&quot; matcher=&quot;regexp&quot; module=&quot;(commons-logging|logback|log4j-over|slf4j-(?!api|log4j)).*&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/dependencies&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivy-module&gt;<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;2.0&quot;<br/>
  xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;<br/>
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=&quot;http://ant.apache.org/ivy/schemas/ivy.xsd&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;info module=&quot;B&quot; organisation=&quot;com.org&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;extends module=&quot;A&quot; organisation=&quot;com.org&quot;<br/>
      extendType=&quot;configurations,dependencies&quot; location=&quot;../A/ivy.xml&quot; revision=&quot;latest&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;dependencies defaultconf=&quot;master&quot; defaultconfmapping=&quot;*-&gt;master,runtime()&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;dependency ... conf=&quot;local&quot; /&gt;&lt;!-- this dependency includes commons-logging transitively and the exclude from module A should stop that from coming in so that jcl-over-slf4j is used instead --&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/dependencies&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/info&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivy-module&gt;<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
Also, if the dependency here defined in B was moved up to A, the exclude properly removes commons-logging from A&#39;s libraries.  But commons-logging will appear in B&#39;s libraries.
  </td>
