                                            <td class="description">      In projects with a lot of configurations (about 200)  and  a lot of dependencies (&gt; 100) the mechanism that (recursively) resolves the conflicts can be VERY expensive due to the combinatorial explosion of the dependencies trees.<br/>
<br/>
In these cases it can be helpful to have a configuration parameter that can be used to completely disable the conflict resolution (using the &quot;all&quot; conflict manager do not help).
