                <tr id="issuerow12895922" rel="12895922" data-issuekey="IVY-1533" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-1533" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-1533">IVY-1533</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Build seems to work, but lots of warning messages about &#39;impossible to put metadata file in cache&#39;
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            David Goblirsch
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            David Goblirsch
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Sep/15 21:59 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Sep/15 21:59 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.4.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      RedHat 6.5 enterprise linux
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Just upgraded from ivy 2.3 to ivy 2.4. Seems to work fine, but even though the end results of the build appear to be the same as when using 2.3, the log is now peppered with lots of warnings of the form<br/>
<br/>
    impossible to put metadata file in cache: [filename] <br/>
<br/>
<br/>
for the ivy:resolve task, raising a &#39;FileNotFoundException&#39; for files with a<br/>
name following this pattern:<br/>
<br/>
  .ivy2/cache/[org]/[name]/ivy-[yyyyMMddHHmmss].xml.original<br/>
<br/>
where [org] is the org of a dependency, [name] is the name of the<br/>
dependency.<br/>
<br/>
The complaint is for our local jars which do not have version numbers.<br/>
It is not observed (yet) for 3rd-party jars having version numbers.<br/>
<br/>
That is, if I build 3 of our local jars A, B, C, and then build a jar D that<br/>
depends on those, the log for D complains  3 times about &#39;impossible to put metadata file in cache: &#39;, for files named ivy-[timestamp].xml.original,<br/>
one message for each of the libraries A, B and C.
  </td>
